<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guangxu Emperor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Guangxu Emperor was a late ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> who reigned in the late nineteenth century under the strong influence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empress-dowager-cixi">Empress Dowager Cixi</a>. In 1898 he backed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days' Reform</a>, which was halted by a conservative coup, after which he was kept under house arrest. His failed reforms are a key episode in the decline of the Qing Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guangxu-emperor.jpg" alt="Guangxu Emperor" width="301" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%85%89%E7%BB%AA%E5%B8%9D.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
